     "legendFormat": "in-cluster (gw <-> srv)"
    },
    {
     "refId": "C",
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "esq-prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "1000 * ((sum(rate(esq_srv_outer_seconds_sum[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(esq_srv_outer_seconds_count[5m])), 1)) - ((sum(rate(esq_srv_inner_seconds_sum[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(esq_srv_inner_seconds_count[5m])), 1)) or vector(0)))",
     "legendFormat": "srv self (compute)"
    },
    {
     "refId": "D",
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "esq-prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "1000 * ((sum(rate(esq_srv_inner_seconds_sum[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(esq_srv_inner_seconds_count[5m])), 1)) or vector(0))",
     "legendFormat": "srv inner (db)"
    }
   ],
   "description": "The four raw timers SUBTRACTED into the bands they imply: net = gw.outer - gw.inner; in-cluster = gw.inner - srv.outer; srv self = srv.outer - srv.inner; srv inner = DB time. Fully aggregated (scalars) on purpose: the gw timers are tagged application=gateway and the srv timers application=<service>, so they cannot be subtracted label-wise. The DB band is STEADY-STATE: the JPA time is collected on every request while observability is on, so it no longer depends on the X-Capture-Metrics load-test header."
